From 005c18c1f4635a8fd5010c1933614ec1af3e46bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:13:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] drama: the backbone chain launches with programmatic
 dependent launch

Every backbone and GDN kernel waits on its predecessor before touching global memory, so it can launch as the one
before it drains. PDL is used only when both backbone images carry the drama_pdl marker, which Module.holds reads,
so an older or mixed prebuilt image set launches plain. tf-cuda-test drama-pdl checks that decision for the
embedded images and for a kernel directory.
